Andaz means "personal style" in Hindi. Andaz Amsterdam Prinsengracht means, five-star creative luxury in the heart of Amsterdam, expressed through local experiences, art & design and picture-perfect drinking and dining, in a playful Dutch-inspired environment.

We are looking for a Finance Intern!

‘Are you looking for an internship that will give you a full understanding of the concept of a hotel?'

YES, because you want&hellip;
• to want to assist Finance team with their day-to-day activities, such as processing workflow analysis and optimization, assisting with month-end financial reports and auditing department budget-to-actual expenses;
• to work on finance related projects;
• to work in a dynamic team;
• to be responsible for Accounts Receivables: sending invoices to third party companies and suppliers;
• to be knowledgeable about all financial systems: Opera, IScala, Micros and Birchstreet. What's in it for YOU?
• a great place to work in the beautiful city center of Amsterdam, right by the canals;
• an entry into the World of Hyatt, where internships may lead into jobs;
• international working experience;
• great intern working conditions (read: EUR 750 monthly allowance, meal per shift, uniform/laundry access, loads of training opportunities, potential career planning, discounts all over the world and let's not forget about our social activities&hellip;!)

Functie-eisen:
And you are&hellip;
• currently enrolled in a Hospitality or Finance related study program;
• always seeking for opportunities and creative solutions;
• hands-on, pro-active and enthusiastic;
• available for five months or longer;
• not afraid to make decisions;
• detail-oriented and approachable;
• very communicative in English and ideally also in Dutch;
• legally allowed to work in the Netherlands, holding an EU/EEA passport or enrolled in a Dutch Institution (we do not assist with Visa / permit applications). 
.. then please upload your CV, the required start- and end date

Are you ready to make an impact in one of the largest warehouses in the Benelux? In this role, you will work at a brand-new, large-scale site that is currently undergoing significant development. The operation is growing rapidly, many new colleagues are joining, and processes are being further built and refined. This requires strong supervisors who can bring structure, direction, and clarity to the operation.

As a Warehouse Supervisor, you are the key link between the team leaders on the floor and the warehouse manager. You will indirectly lead a large group of employees and ensure that daily operations run smoothly, efficiently, and according to agreed standards. You will work in an environment where structure is essential and processes must be strictly followed from A to Z. At the same time, you are the one who maintains oversight, makes adjustments, and takes decisions when necessary.

Your responsibilities:

- Leading and supporting multiple team leaders and their teams;
- Monitoring daily operations, planning, and performance;
- Conducting conversations regarding absenteeism, performance, and employee development;
- Justifying operational decisions towards warehouse management (such as capacity and overtime);
- Ensuring strict adherence to processes and procedures;
- Monitoring KPIs, quality, and operational progress;
- Coordinating with different departments and internal stakeholders;
- Identifying bottlenecks and implementing improvements ;
- Working with reports and administrative processes (including Excel).

For this position, we are looking for a strong and experienced supervisor who is used to working in a high-paced, operational warehouse environment.

